\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  Jesus Christ, my sure defence
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  and my Saviour, ever liveth,
\par  Knowing this, my confidence
\par  rests upon the hope it giveth,
\par  tho' the night of death be fraught
\par  still with many anxious thought.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li270\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.   Jesus, my Redeemer, lives;
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0  I too, unto life must waken;
\par  He will fetch me where He is,
\par  Shall my courage then be shaken?
\par \i  Shall I fear or could the Head
\par  rise and leave its members dead?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\i0\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.  Nay too closely am I bound
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 unto Him by hope for ever;
\par faith's strong hand the rock has found,
\par grasped it and will leave it never,
\par Not the ban of death can part
\par  from its Lord the trusting heart.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Dust I am and must therefore
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Once again return to ashes
\par This I know, He is the door,\tab 
\par the fulfillment of all wishes.
\par Oh! that I eternally
\par \pard        may with my dear Saviour be!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

